[{ "action": "append", "id": "event-modals", "value" : "<div tabindex=\"-1\" id=\"modal-045f9966-cdbb-4d7a-87d5-1197fc61560c\" class=\"modal\"><div class=\"modal-dialog modal-lg\"><div class=\"modal-content\"><div class=\"modal-header\"><a data-dismiss=\"modal\" class=\"close\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-remove\"></span></a><p class=\"text-muted\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-road\"></span> Research Track</p><strong>Wed 15 Apr 2026 16:30 - 16:45 at <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/room/icse-2026/icse-2026-venue-oceania-x\" class=\"room-link navigate\">Oceania X</a></strong> - <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/track/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track#program\" class=\"navigate\">Dependability and Security 3</a> <small>Chair(s): <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2026/larsgrunske\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\">Lars Grunske</a></small></div><div class=\"modal-body\"><div class=\"bg-primary event-title\"><h4><span data-event-star=\"045f9966-cdbb-4d7a-87d5-1197fc61560c\" title=\"Add event to your program\"><span class=\"text-disabled glyphicon glyphicon-star-empty\"></span></span><strong>One Size Does Fit All: Kernel-Assisted Fine-Grained Debloating and Layout Randomization for Shared Libraries</strong></h4></div><div class=\"bg-info event-description\"><p>Prevalent software engineering practices, such as code reuse and the \u201Cone-size-fits-all\u201D methodology, have significantly contributed to code bloat. Code debloating, which targets the reduction of extraneous code, emerges as a promising solution to combat this issue. However, current methods that depend on redundant code deletion are at odds with the foundational design philosophy of reusable code components, regardless of whether they are applied offline or at runtime.</p>\n<p>In this paper, we introduce a kernel-assisted debloating framework, K-Polarizer, that aligns with the \u201Cone-size-fits-all\u201D design philosophy of shared libraries. Starting from scratch, K-Polarizer progressively appends dependencies on demand to the underlying page cache associated with offline-reconstructed shared libraries, enabling it to practice the hybrid debloating strategy of \u201Ccutting unwanted pages while loading needed functions.\u201D This allows for code sharing among processes while minimizing the global code base, keeping the visible code base for each process to an approximate minimum. Additionally, K-Polarizer integrates layout randomization at load-time to enhance security further. We have thoroughly evaluated K-Polarizer using real-world shared libraries, including musl-libc, glibc, and libFLAC. The results indicate that K-Polarizer operates transparently, preserving the original functionality of the libraries. Furthermore, K-Polarizer provides security guarantees (76.1% gadget reduction on musl-libc) comparable to the leading debloating technique with acceptable overhead, while gracefully handling the scenario of dynamic library loading. Meanwhile, it offers resilience against memory disclosures.</p>\n<p></p><p></p><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2026/ziyilin\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Ziyi Lin<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Xidian University</span></h5></div></div></a></div><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2026/haoyuma\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Haoyu Ma<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Beijing Jiaotong University</span></h5></div></div></a></div></div><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2026/kexinliu\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Kexin Liu<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Nankai University</span></h5></div></div></a></div><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2026/bowenli2\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Bowen Li<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Xidian University</span></h5></div></div></a></div></div><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2026/jinkuli\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Jinku Li<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Xidian University</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>China</small></h5></div></div></a></div><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2026/jianfengma\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Jianfeng Ma<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Xidian University</span></h5></div></div></a></div></div></div><br></div><div class=\"modal-footer\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/110/One-Size-Does-Fit-All-Kernel-Assisted-Fine-Grained-Debloating-and-Layout-Randomizati\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"btn btn-default navigate\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-new-window\"></span> All Details</a></span><a href=\"#\" data-dismiss=\"modal\" class=\"btn btn-default\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-remove\"></span> Close</a></div></div></div></div>"},{ "action": "runscript", "value": "$('#modal-045f9966-cdbb-4d7a-87d5-1197fc61560c').modal({ backdrop: 'static', keyboard: true}, 'show');" },
